      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn `amd_march`, `Scheduler.init_all_cuda_graphs` runs without `torch.no_grad()`, so tensors made during CUDA graph capture carry autograd state. This bites the ROCm MoE path without aiter. There, `fused_experts` reduces with `moe_sum_reduce_torch_compile`, which is `torch.sum(..., out=...)` under `torch.compile`, and that op refuses out= when an argument requires grad. Decode CUDA graph capture of any MoE model then fails and the scheduler dies:\n\n```\ntorch._dynamo.exc.TorchRuntimeError: RuntimeError when making fake tensor call\n... got RuntimeError(\"sum(): functions with out=... arguments don't support automatic differentiation, but one of the arguments requires grad.\")\n  File \".../moe_runner/triton_utils/fused_moe.py\", line 372, in moe_sum_reduce_torch_compile\n  File \".../runner/decode_cuda_graph_runner.py\", line 492, in __init__\n```\n\n`main` already fixed this in #43854 (`@torch.no_grad()` on `init_all_cuda_graphs`). This PR is a clean `git cherry-pick -x` of it, with authorship kept. Found while validating RDNA on `amd_march` (#46900).\n\n## Modifications\n\nCherry-pick of b60444c621 (#43854): `python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py`, +3 lines.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nallenai/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct on a Radeon AI PRO R9700 (gfx1201), TP1. Environment: no aiter; vLLM not importable, so RMSNorm uses `forward_native`. Applied on top of #46914, which is needed to import without aiter. Accuracy: `sgl-eval==0.1.2` gsm8k, 200 examples, temperature 0.7, top_p 0.8.\n\n| config | result |\n|---|---|\n| `amd_march` + #46914, default (decode CUDA graph) | scheduler dies during graph capture (trace above) |\n| `amd_march` + #46914, `--disable-cuda-graph` | serves; gsm8k 0.585 |\n| `amd_march` + #46914 + this PR, default | decode graph captured in 4.8 s; gsm8k 0.605 |\n\nOn a Radeon PRO W7900D (gfx1100), vLLM 0.31 / torch 2.13, with #46914 + #46915 + this PR at default flags, the same model serves with the decode CUDA graph captured: gsm8k 0.545 on the same harness.\n\nI only exercised MoE on RDNA. The change itself is the one `main` already carries for all platforms.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A (capture-time grad mode only).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Backport; covered upstream by #43854.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No doc change needed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results. (See above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40643270024](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40643270024)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40643269947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40643269947)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40643270007](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40643270007)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
