  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "@HaiShaw this is another clean backport from `main` (#43854). Without it, on `amd_march` any MoE model running without aiter dies during decode CUDA graph capture. cc @ix-48 as the original author.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-28T06:20:40Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46967#issuecomment-6462222352",
      "id": 6462222352,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-28T06:20:40Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vivienfanghuagood"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@sogalin @hubertlu-tw another clean cherry-pick from `main` (#43854, +3 lines). Without it, MoE models on ROCm without aiter crash during decode CUDA graph capture on `amd_march`. With it, OLMoE serves with graphs on gfx1100 and gfx1201. Could you review?\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T07:34:01Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46967#issuecomment-6490792684",
      "id": 6490792684,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T07:34:01Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vivienfanghuagood"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "CI evidence (gfx1201, stock `rocm/pytorch` image, no aiter): a daily run of `amd_march` with this PR stacked on top together with #46910, #46914, #46915, #46967 and #46909 passes every step ([run](https://github.com/vivienfanghuagood/sglang/actions/runs/40852621154)). The same run on plain `amd_march` fails ([run](https://github.com/vivienfanghuagood/sglang/actions/runs/40852611904)). For this PR: OLMoE (MoE) serves with decode CUDA graphs with the stack (gsm8k 66% on 50 questions); on `amd_march` it can't start at all (aiter import).\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T10:16:14Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46967#issuecomment-6493973554",
      "id": 6493973554,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T10:16:14Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vivienfanghuagood"
      }
    }
